1
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:03,545
[BILLY] <i>Melissa and Theo.</i>

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:06,464
<i>A cute and happy couple, at first glance.</i>

3
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:09,551
<i>I got to talk to her,</i>
<i>and she mentioned that</i>

4
00:00:09,634 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>Melissa's dad believes that Theo</i>
<i>doesn't deserve his daughter.</i>

5
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:19,602
<i>They will push through with the wedding,</i>
<i>with or without the father's blessing.</i>

6
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:22,605
- [TONI]<i> Chief, this is so beautiful!</i>
- [BILLY]<i> Mm-hmm!</i>

7
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:24,065
<i>This is hand-painted?</i>

8
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,442
<i>The artist did amazing, huh?</i>

9
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:28,361
<i>Yeah! I wonder who the painter is?</i>

10
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:29,904
[YANI] <i>I'm sorry.</i>

11
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:33,116
<i>I realized too late that</i>
<i>when you love someone,</i>

12
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:35,368
<i>you must also love</i>
<i>the things they hold dear.</i>

13
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:38,955
[CAMILLE] <i>Bea, I really love</i>
<i>the last-minute revisions.</i>

14
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:41,916
<i>So minimalist. So modern.</i>

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>This was their dream wedding, after all,</i>

16
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:45,754
<i>so we made it happen for them.</i>

17
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,257
- [MELISSA]<i> You know, I'm an only child.</i>
- [BILLY]<i> Mm-hmm.</i>

18
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:50,675
<i>And I'm a daddy's girl.</i>

19
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:53,720
<i>And the only reason</i>
<i>I believe in fairytales</i>

20
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:57,807
<i>is because growing up,</i>
<i>my dad made everything possible.</i>

21
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:01,478
<i>Except for the most important thing to me.</i>

22
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:04,355
<i>His presence at my wedding.</i>
[SOFT SOB]

23
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,611
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

24
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:15,909
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

25
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,702
<i>Theo.</i>

26
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:20,580
<i>May your happily ever after</i>

27
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:23,541
<i>begin with my blessing.</i>

28
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,920
[CELEBRANT] <i>Dear friends and family,</i>

29
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:29,964
<i>we are gathered here today</i>

30
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:34,511
<i>to celebrate the union</i>
<i>of Theo and Melissa.</i>

31
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:37,388
[MELISSA] <i>My Theo,</i>
<i>I promise to be your home, your heart,</i>

32
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:38,973
<i>and your endless adventure,</i>

33
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:41,142
<i>now and for all the days to come.</i>

34
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,519
[THEO] <i>Melissa,</i>

35
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:44,229
<i>I vow to walk beside you</i>

36
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:46,397
<i>through every dream and every storm,</i>

37
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:48,817
<i>as your love lights the path before us.</i>

38
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,985
[CELEBRANT] <i>By the power vested in me,</i>

39
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:54,823
<i>and in the presence</i>
<i>of your family and friends,</i>

40
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:57,242
<i>I now pronounce you</i>

41
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:59,702
<i>husband and wife.</i>

42
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:03,331
<i>Theo, you may kiss your bride.</i>

43
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:09,420
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

44
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,464
[MORRIE]<i> Excuse me.</i>

45
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:12,715
<i>What are you watching?</i>

46
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,467
[GUEST] <i>The Happily Ever After event.</i>

47
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,511
<i>What the hell is Happily Ever After?</i>

48
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:18,555
<i>LoveList's event.</i>

49
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,724
<i>Their live stream has</i>
<i>500,000 views.</i>

50
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:22,851
<i>How many do we have?</i>

51
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:24,477
[MORRIE] <i>Twelve thousand, Ms. Camille.</i>

52
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:26,771
[CAMILLE] <i>Only 12,000 views.</i>

53
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:27,939
<i>God!</i>

54
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:36,447
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

55
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,577
Boss.

56
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:41,995
Good job.

57
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:43,163
- Cheers.
- Thank you.

58
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,539
Good job to you too.

59
00:02:50,753 --> 00:02:54,841
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:55,758
Billy?

61
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:56,926
Sir.

62
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,637
I received this earlier.

63
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,639
[MELISSA ON VIDEO]
<i>You know, I'm an only child.</i>

64
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:03,600
<i>And I'm a daddy's girl.</i>

65
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:06,060
<i>And the only reason</i>
<i>I believe in fairytales</i>

66
00:03:06,144 --> 00:03:10,648
<i>is because growing up,</i>
<i>my dad made everything possible.</i>

67
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,692
<i>For me, his princess.</i>

68
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:15,612
<i>You know, he gave me everything I wanted.</i>

69
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:19,073
<i>Except for the most important thing to me.</i>

70
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:21,492
<i>His presence at my wedding.</i>

71
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:25,121
It's true. She's a daddy's girl.

72
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:30,293
She told me it was your idea
to send this to me,

73
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:33,338
and… I couldn't thank you enough.

74
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,757
If it wasn't for this,

75
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:38,218
I wouldn't be here today.

76
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:44,098
And I would have regretted it
for the rest of my life,

77
00:03:44,182 --> 00:03:47,143
knowing that I hurt

78
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:50,980
my beloved daughter on her special day.

79
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:57,528
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

80
00:03:57,612 --> 00:04:01,241
Melissa is very lucky
to have a father like you.

81
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:07,080
You all deserve a happily ever after.

82
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:10,541
Thank you so much.

83
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:11,501
Thank you, thank you.

84
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:14,128
- It's the best.
- Congratulations, ma'am!

85
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:15,213
[HAZEL] Thank you so much!

86
00:04:15,838 --> 00:04:17,382
- Sir, thank you so much.
- Thank you.

87
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:19,300
- Thank you so much.
- [JORDAN] No, it's our pleasure.

88
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,636
- We will recommend, definitely.
- We're very happy for you guys.

89
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:22,553
Thank you very much.

90
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:25,181
- Go, enjoy your party.
- Thank you.

91
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,516
- [HAZEL] You too!
- Yeah.

92
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:27,934
[BILLY] Cheers!

93
00:04:28,017 --> 00:04:29,394
[HAZEL GIGGLING]

94
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:30,395
[GLASSES CLINK]

95
00:04:30,478 --> 00:04:32,814
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

96
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:34,691
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

97
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:36,234
Let's go!

98
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:38,194
- Come on, CEO!
- [WOMAN WHOOPING]

99
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:44,534
[GUESTS WHOOPING]

100
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:45,618
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

101
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:46,869
Come on, let's go!

102
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:51,207
[GUEST] Yeah!

103
00:04:54,836 --> 00:05:00,717
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

104
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,963
- [UPBEAT MUSIC OVER SPEAKERS]
- [ROBBIE] Oh, ma'am!

105
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,758
Uh… Red wine! Red wine, right?

106
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,634
Yes, ma'am. For you.

107
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:45,428
[VALERIE] Thank you.

108
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:51,768
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

109
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:53,352
- I didn't expect to see you!
- Rain?

110
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:54,520
- Rain?
- Can I have a drink?

111
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,564
Come here. My eyes hurt,
so take over for now.

112
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:57,982
[BLAIRE] You're so cute!

113
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:00,026
Yes, Ms. Blaire? Can I have your order?

114
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:04,155
I want a drink, but I want him
to serve it to me.

115
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:06,032
- He's busy. I'll do it.
- No!

116
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:08,201
[BLAIRE] You're so funny.

117
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:10,119
Thank you.

118
00:06:11,412 --> 00:06:12,246
Wow.

119
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:15,374
You really gave Melissa
her happily ever after.

120
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:17,668
You know, I was thinking,

121
00:06:19,337 --> 00:06:21,631
I wish my mother had had that too.

122
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:23,883
- [TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]
- Had what?

123
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:27,470
A happily ever after.

124
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,642
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER, LAUGHTER]

125
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:34,018
I like to think

126
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:37,105
she's happily watching over you,

127
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,398
proud of you and Oliver.

128
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:42,944
Maybe.

129
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,570
Pretty amazing, right?

130
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:47,406
It's so fulfilling to think that

131
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:50,368
we get to do something this meaningful.

132
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:53,287
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:55,331
We make love happen.

134
00:06:58,543 --> 00:06:59,752
Make love happen.

135
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:01,963
[GLASSES CLINK]

136
00:07:03,297 --> 00:07:05,508
[MUSIC FADING]

137
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:11,848
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:24,652
[INTENSE DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,414
[MUSIC FADING]

140
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:40,835
[LIVELY MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

141
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:43,296
[BILLY] Came here to take notes?

142
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:47,258
[DRYLY] You win.

143
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:51,137
In a way, I should actually thank you.

144
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,183
If you hadn't stolen LoveFeast,

145
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:58,269
I wouldn't have thought
of something much better.

146
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:01,272
Really?

147
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:04,317
Okay, then.

148
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,360
I did steal it.

149
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,988
But the question is,

150
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:13,034
which one of us is the bigger thief?

151
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:14,619
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:15,995
A thief?

153
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,582
What the hell are you talking about?

154
00:08:21,792 --> 00:08:23,211
If only you knew.

155
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,755
Knew what?

156
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,843
Why don't you just tell the truth,

157
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:33,596
so I can understand
where your anger is coming from?

158
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:37,016
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

159
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:39,602
What's your reason for going after me?

160
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:42,188
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

161
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:48,945
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,745
[MUSIC FADING]

163
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:02,875
Can you believe it?

164
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:05,545
She dared to show her face here.

165
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:08,506
Luckily, she didn't do anything
to ruin the event.

166
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:10,424
I would've loved to see her try.

167
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:14,679
I'm sure she just came here to spy on us.

168
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:17,890
[JORDAN] But this time,
she can't steal our plan.

169
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:20,726
[BILLY] Absolutely not.
Dude, that's top secret.

170
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:24,188
Hearts Island will be
our next biggest project.

171
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:26,190
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,692
Can we really pull it off?

173
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:30,236
Oh, come on. You're still doubting?

174
00:09:31,195 --> 00:09:32,363
Let's make a bet.

175
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,657
- I can't win against you.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

176
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:38,202
Imagine.

177
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,038
Twenty single women…

178
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:43,499
- This summer.
- This summer.

179
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,126
Catchy, right?

180
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:48,004
I love it.

181
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:53,342
- [MUSIC FADING]
- [CITY NOISE]

182
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,136
[BEA] Pebblng's newest offering?

183
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:58,139
We'll choose 20 women searchers,

184
00:09:58,222 --> 00:10:01,767
and we will bring them
to a romantic island,

185
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:05,313
which we'll call Hearts Island.

186
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:08,733
Then a group of 20 single men will arrive.

187
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:14,322
For one week,
they'll bond and go on dates.

188
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:17,491
Through it all,
we'll see who has chemistry,

189
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:21,120
and who's the perfect match!

190
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:24,540
This is going to beat LoveList for sure.

191
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:26,542
This better be.

192
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,377
Because LoveFeast cost us a lot.

193
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:30,838
And the numbers didn't justify it.

194
00:10:30,921 --> 00:10:34,842
Memberships, revenue, impact…

195
00:10:34,925 --> 00:10:36,427
None of it translated!

196
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:38,346
To be honest,

197
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,514
the mediocre execution

198
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:43,517
compared to Happily Ever After's

199
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:46,228
did not elevate our brand.

200
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:47,855
I promise you,

201
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:49,523
this time, we're coming back stronger.

202
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:51,651
I'm gonna make sure everything is perfect.

203
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,194
Okay, wait.

204
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:56,697
Why is this one a carbon copy of that?

205
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:59,867
It's called exactly the same!
<i>Hearts Island!</i>

206
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:04,038
It's a reality TV show
in the US that flopped!

207
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:05,873
[BEA CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]
That's impossible.

208
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:07,583
[CAMILLE] Sorry. May I see?

209
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,834
[LINDSAY SIGHS]

210
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:10,920
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:14,090
[FEMALE VO] <i>This summer,</i>
<i>we're taking love to paradise!</i>

212
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:17,093
<i>Twenty single women, twenty single men.</i>

213
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:19,678
<i>One romantic island.</i>

214
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,972
<i>Seven days to connect, to date,</i>

215
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:25,559
<i>and to discover</i>
<i>what real connection feels like.</i>

216
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:28,270
<i>Welcome to </i>Hearts Island!

217
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:29,939
Ms. Camille…

218
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:32,316
It's probably just a coincidence. Um…

219
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,652
[BEA STAMMERS] I didn't know--

220
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:36,612
I didn't know that was a thing.

221
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:38,364
It's the same concept.

222
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:39,865
Even the title!

223
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:41,909
It makes me wonder.

224
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:43,452
Maybe Billy was right.

225
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:46,914
That LoveFeast was really
a LoveList original.

226
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:49,333
This Hearts Island project, Bea.

227
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:52,086
Is this another stolen idea by Pebblng?

228
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:53,879
Is it?

229
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:57,383
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

230
00:11:57,466 --> 00:11:58,342
[GLASS THUDS]

231
00:11:58,426 --> 00:12:01,053
- A waste of my time and money.
- Ma'am, I'm so sorry.

232
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,389
I promise you,
I will get to the bottom of this,

233
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:05,516
and I will fix everything.

234
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:07,393
You were spot on.

235
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:08,686
Bea took the bait.

236
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:11,772
So she actually presented it
to Pebblng's investors?

237
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,149
Yes, Ms. Billy.

238
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,151
And she was even confident presenting it,

239
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:18,320
not knowing her pitch had
already been produced.

240
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,447
So funny.

241
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,365
She didn't even bother
to research properly.

242
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:22,616
[BILLY, DRYLY] <i>Oh my.</i>

243
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,870
She has become too predictable.

244
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:28,247
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,331
Thank you, Morrie.

246
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:30,791
No, Ms. Billy. Thank you.

247
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:33,502
Because, honestly,
the moment she joined Pebblng,

248
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:36,547
I already felt that something
was off about her.

249
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,216
But, of course, I had to give her
the benefit of the doubt.

250
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:42,887
Then word got out that
she was using her dead sister's name.

251
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:45,598
And yet, Ms. Camille still helped her.

252
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:48,100
After that, I said to myself,

253
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:49,685
"This is wrong. It's unfair."

254
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:51,562
That's why you came to me.

255
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:54,648
Because I knew I needed
your help, Ms. Billy.

256
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,317
So, thank you.

257
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:02,072
[BEA] I knew it! You're a snake!

258
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:03,032
A snake!

259
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:04,867
Wait, I'm the snake?

260
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:07,828
Of the two of us,
who's the fraud and the liar?

261
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:09,121
You!

262
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:10,039
- [GRUNTS]
- [SLAPS]

263
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:11,081
- [SLAPS]
- [GROANS]

264
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:12,416
You bastard! The nerve--

265
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,792
- You dare hit me, huh?!
- Stop!

266
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,628
- I knew I couldn't trust you!
- Bea, stop this!

267
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:17,713
- Argh!
- Thought I wouldn't fight back?!

268
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:19,131
Well, I will!

269
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:21,383
- [BEA GRUNTS] Get off me--
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:22,635
[CAMILLE] Stop it!

271
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:24,887
[BEA] Ouch, Morrie! You're hurting me!

272
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:26,680
- Ms. Camille--
- Morrie…

273
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,057
[BEA] How dare you, Morrie?!

274
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,351
- You actually hurt me!
- You! My office, now!

275
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:32,061
Yes, Ms. Camille. [FAKE CRYING]

276
00:13:32,144 --> 00:13:34,730
I… I can't believe Morrie did that.

277
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:36,482
[GRUNTS]

278
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:37,858
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

279
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:39,485
[THROUGH GRITTED TEETH]
Remember this!

280
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,404
Snake!

281
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,407
[MUSIC ENDS]

282
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:49,453
Ms. Camille, I honestly didn't know
such a show even existed.

283
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,580
And with the same concept too.

284
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,791
I had absolutely no idea.

285
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:58,462
Then I found out that Billy and Morrie
were in cahoots!

286
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:03,592
Earlier, when Morrie realized
I overheard their conversation,

287
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:07,096
he lunged at me right away
and started hitting me!

288
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:09,515
Ms. Camille, he even threatened me!

289
00:14:09,598 --> 00:14:11,433
- [CAMILLE] That's enough.
- His exact words were…

290
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,310
Bea, that's enough.

291
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:15,312
You don't have to explain.

292
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:21,277
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:26,740
You also don't have to give back
your salary advance.

294
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:27,992
You can have it.

295
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:30,744
Thank you, ma'am.

296
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,663
Get out of my office.

297
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:35,165
And get out of my company!

298
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:37,710
What?

299
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:39,587
Ms. Camille…

300
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:40,921
Why?

301
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,674
What for? I didn't do anything wrong!

302
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:45,467
I'm not lying! Believe me!

303
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:47,344
I could never lie to you!

304
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:50,180
[BILLY IN RECORDING] <i>In a way,</i>
<i>I should actually thank you.</i>

305
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:54,226
<i>If you hadn't stolen LoveFeast,</i>

306
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,563
<i>I wouldn't have thought</i>
<i>of something much better.</i>

307
00:14:57,646 --> 00:14:59,440
[BEA IN RECORDING] <i>Okay, then.</i>

308
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,025
<i>I did steal it.</i>

309
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:02,484
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

310
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:05,112
Who was that? That wasn't me!

311
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:07,323
That's fake! It wasn't my voice!

312
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:10,200
I'd never say those things!
It's obviously fake!

313
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,536
I'd never do-- I'd never say any of that!

314
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:15,247
Bea! You're the fake one!

315
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,917
Everything about you is fake.

316
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,418
But this is my fault.

317
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:24,089
I let my competitiveness get in the way
because I wanted to take down LoveList.

318
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,884
But my biggest mistake was trusting you.

319
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:28,302
Um…

320
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:30,596
Ms. Camille, please! Please, please!

321
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:33,641
Believe me! That wasn't me!
It's totally fake!

322
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:35,684
I could never lie!
Please, give me one more--

323
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:37,645
Bea, go!

324
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:38,729
Goodbye!

325
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:40,689
Ms. Camille, please! Please!

326
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:43,984
Besides, you can't just fire
someone on a whim!

327
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,110
You can't do that!

328
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:48,197
On grounds of falsification
of documents and fraud alone,

329
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,824
I have more than enough reason
to fire you, Bea!

330
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,576
So, go! Get out!

331
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:53,702
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

332
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:55,913
[SIGHS] I should've listened to Billy.

333
00:15:58,165 --> 00:15:59,291
Billy?

334
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:01,961
Seriously? You too?

335
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:04,838
Billy this, Billy that! It's always Billy!

336
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:09,468
You want to believe that Billy?
Then go ahead, believe her!

337
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:12,137
Mark my words.

338
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:14,014
It's your loss.

339
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:16,558
You made a big mistake firing me.

340
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:19,353
You and Billy…

341
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:21,271
You deserve each other!

342
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:24,066
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

343
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:25,567
- What?!
- [EMPLOYEE] Whoa!

344
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:30,155
[SCOFFS]

345
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:31,407
Happy now?

346
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:34,535
Jealous bastard!

347
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:39,206
- [BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]
- [MUSIC FADING]

348
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:42,543
[PHONE CHIMES]

349
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:45,754
[PHONE CHIMES]

350
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:49,216
[PHONE CHIMES]

351
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:52,094
[PHONE CHIMES]

352
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:58,142
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:16:58,225 --> 00:16:59,435
- [CONFETTI POPS]
- [SHRIEKS]

354
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:01,687
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

355
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,148
- Wow! A surprise for me!
- Yes, yes!

356
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:07,151
- Thank you! Oh, thank you!
- Congratulations!

357
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,569
Thank you!

358
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:09,987
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

359
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:12,281
[BILLY] Wow! You actually went all-out!

360
00:17:12,364 --> 00:17:14,491
How sweet! Thank you!

361
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:17,453
And of course,
congratulations to all of us.

362
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:19,163
And of course…

363
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:22,416
- Congratulations, Blaire!
- [TONI] There we go!

364
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:26,253
[BLAIRE] That's why we want
to thank you, chief.

365
00:17:26,336 --> 00:17:29,465
On behalf of all
the contractual employees,

366
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:30,966
thank you so much.

367
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:34,094
You didn't just renew our contracts.

368
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:36,138
You made us regular employees!

369
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,806
Of course.

370
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:39,683
- [TONI] Aww.
- [SQUEALS]

371
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:41,602
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

372
00:17:41,685 --> 00:17:43,937
We've been through so much together.

373
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,732
Late nights. Tight headlines.

374
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:51,612
<i>Moments when it felt like</i>
<i>everything was just against us.</i>

375
00:17:52,237 --> 00:17:54,239
But you all stayed.

376
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:55,866
You're still here.

377
00:17:55,949 --> 00:17:57,284
You stayed.

378
00:17:57,367 --> 00:17:58,744
You fought for us.

379
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:00,454
For LoveList.

380
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:02,289
So thank you.

381
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:06,001
As you all know,
I don't just see you as my team.

382
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:08,128
Here, we're a family.

383
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:11,090
And in this family,
no one gets left behind.

384
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,383
So I promise,

385
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,219
we'll keep growing.

386
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:18,597
We'll keep making this family stronger.

387
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,015
Together.

388
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:24,061
- Together!
- Together!

389
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:27,314
[ALL CHANTING] LoveList!
LoveList! LoveList! LoveList!

390
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:30,109
- [BILLY] Oh, wow! Let me take a picture!
- LoveList! LoveList!

391
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,652
- Wow!
- LoveList! LoveList!

392
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:33,654
- Congrats, everyone!
- [TONI] Yay!

393
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,280
- Group hug!
- Group hug!

394
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,323
- Yes!
- Come closer!

395
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:37,783
Come on, everyone!

396
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:39,868
- [FOND NOISES]
- [MUSIC FADES]

397
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,453
[TRAFFIC NOISE IN DISTANCE]

398
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:49,086
[DOCTOR] Mr. Toledo is cleared
for discharge.

399
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:51,547
He may now be transferred
into your custody.

400
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:52,923
[POLICE OFFICER] Okay, Doc.

401
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:54,299
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

402
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:58,679
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

403
00:19:03,058 --> 00:19:05,686
- [THWACKING]
- [GRUNTING, GROANING]

404
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:07,771
[BEA] <i>We have</i>
<i>a lot of work to do.</i>

405
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,023
<i>What's your wish,</i>
<i>my dear grandson?</i>

406
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:11,525
<i>Happiness for</i>

407
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:13,694
<i>the people I care about most.</i>

408
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:19,491
<i>I suppose it wouldn't hurt</i>
<i>to give her a proper scare.</i>

409
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:21,952
<i>You want to scare her, babe?</i>

410
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:24,705
[ALL SINGING]
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

411
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:26,540
<i>- To me!</i>
- [CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

412
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:29,543
[BILLY] <i>Ever since we were kids, we've</i>
<i>always celebrated our birthdays together.</i>

413
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:32,087
<i>So it can't be just about me.</i>

414
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:34,840
<i>If you're meant to be together,</i>
<i>then you will be. But if not…</i>

415
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:36,300
<i>I guess it's just not meant to happen.</i>

416
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:38,594
<i>- This is for you.</i>
<i>- For me?</i>

417
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:40,888
<i>If it's meant for you,</i>
<i>then you'll have it. Right?</i>

418
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:41,805
<i>Mm-hmm.</i>

419
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:46,310
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

420
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:53,066
<i>♪ When you're crying</i>
<i>And don't know why ♪</i>

421
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:58,030
<i>- ♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>
- [APPLAUSE]

422
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:59,907
<i>Best birthday gift ever.</i>

423
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:02,284
<i>- Happy birthday, dude.</i>
<i>- Thank you.</i>
